1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,000
A sound soul dwells within a sound mind and a sound body.

2
00:00:14,640 --> 00:00:16,560
It's all right, Asherah.

3
00:00:19,680 --> 00:00:23,320
I'll be by your side, watching over you and protecting you.

4
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:26,960
Like this, always and forever.

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:50,000
I'm falling, coming through my shadow.

6
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:54,000
I'm falling, coming through my shadow.

7
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:58,000
I'm falling, coming through my shadow.

8
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:02,000
Stay away,君が望めば

9
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:06,000
どんな世界も

10
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:10,000
その目に映せるから

11
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:14,000
See you in your dreams, yeah, baby

12
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:20,000
怖い夢だとしても

13
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:24,000
テレブル君のために

14
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:28,000
星を砕ぎ

15
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:30,000
飾り付けた

16
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,000
Black paper

17
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:36,000
信じてくれたなら

18
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:38,000
When you

19
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:41,000
Lost in your world

20
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:44,000
Forever with your soul

21
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:46,000
見上がれば

22
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:48,000
輝く

23
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:50,000
月のように

24
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:54,000
Forever with your soul

25
00:01:54,000 --> 00:02:13,700
What's happening?

26
00:02:13,700 --> 00:02:17,280
Everything is so confusing.

27
00:02:19,920 --> 00:02:21,920
There's too much going on at one time.

28
00:02:22,240 --> 00:02:23,560
I can't make sense of it all.

29
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:41,380
And right now, it's difficult to tell

30
00:02:41,380 --> 00:02:43,940
what the Academy's real objective is in all this.

31
00:02:48,340 --> 00:02:53,160
The Kishan's free, and the world is about to be consumed by madness.

32
00:02:53,160 --> 00:03:01,180
That's where our focus should be.

33
00:03:02,560 --> 00:03:07,260
After all, the Academy was founded in the first place to fight the Kishan.

34
00:03:07,260 --> 00:03:12,720
That I understand.

35
00:03:13,860 --> 00:03:15,780
But what about everything else they've done?

36
00:03:16,560 --> 00:03:17,760
What happens now?

37
00:03:17,760 --> 00:03:28,960
Trouble sleeping?

38
00:03:30,880 --> 00:03:31,900
Leave me alone.

39
00:03:37,900 --> 00:03:40,340
Acting like this isn't going to help you out any tomorrow.

40
00:03:40,340 --> 00:03:43,700
The mission's going to be difficult enough as is.

41
00:03:45,900 --> 00:03:46,740
Hey, Sol.

42
00:03:47,400 --> 00:03:47,700
Huh?

43
00:03:49,500 --> 00:03:51,040
Are they doing the right thing?

44
00:03:51,560 --> 00:03:51,880
Huh?

45
00:03:52,540 --> 00:03:53,040
Who?

46
00:03:53,140 --> 00:03:54,200
What are you talking about?

47
00:03:56,060 --> 00:03:57,020
The Academy.

48
00:03:57,760 --> 00:03:59,800
I don't understand what they're doing anymore.

49
00:04:00,600 --> 00:04:03,100
They've completely stopped looking for Professor Stein.

50
00:04:05,080 --> 00:04:07,540
Then there's all that other stuff Kidd told us about.

51
00:04:08,740 --> 00:04:10,300
And also...

52
00:04:10,340 --> 00:04:13,540
What about poor Krona?

53
00:04:13,740 --> 00:04:15,320
He's still locked up in that cell.

54
00:04:16,500 --> 00:04:17,380
No idea.

55
00:04:17,680 --> 00:04:18,880
You know as much as I do.

56
00:04:23,140 --> 00:04:25,500
Sitting in the dark and pouting isn't going to help.

57
00:04:25,840 --> 00:04:26,940
Just get some sleep.

58
00:04:26,940 --> 00:04:38,780
Be careful out there today, you two.

59
00:04:39,540 --> 00:04:39,840
Ha!

60
00:04:40,140 --> 00:04:41,900
We can handle this no problem.

61
00:04:42,100 --> 00:04:44,800
We'll destroy the Kishan and be back before you even know it.

62
00:04:44,800 --> 00:04:49,780
Something wrong?

63
00:04:49,780 --> 00:04:51,740
Don't worry about her.

64
00:04:52,540 --> 00:04:53,820
She'll snap out of it soon.

65
00:04:54,660 --> 00:04:55,400
Hmm.

66
00:04:56,600 --> 00:04:57,760
Let's do this.

67
00:04:57,760 --> 00:05:03,080
Everyone's working so hard to stop this Kishan guy.

68
00:05:03,080 --> 00:05:05,320
I want to help defeat him, too.

69
00:05:06,120 --> 00:05:07,160
Yee-yow!

70
00:05:11,820 --> 00:05:13,620
Charge Baba Yaga's castle.

71
00:05:14,080 --> 00:05:15,280
Things are kind of gloomy.

72
00:05:15,280 --> 00:05:22,580
The objective of today's mission, destroy the Kishan Asherah.

73
00:05:23,080 --> 00:05:29,780
In addition, we will target those who have sided with the Kishan, including the witch Arachne and the members of her organization, Arachnophobia.

74
00:05:29,780 --> 00:05:33,080
We will be launching in a time of our phase of operations.

75
00:05:33,720 --> 00:05:36,040
Cover-ups, repeated without hesitation.

76
00:05:37,480 --> 00:05:40,540
While they turn a blind eye to everything else but their mission.

77
00:05:42,780 --> 00:05:44,600
The madness is spreading.

78
00:05:45,440 --> 00:05:46,680
It must be stopped.

79
00:05:47,500 --> 00:05:48,780
Before it's too late.

80
00:05:49,520 --> 00:05:52,300
Which means we will also be battling against time.

81
00:05:53,200 --> 00:05:55,680
Our first objective, destroy the Kishan.

82
00:05:56,360 --> 00:05:58,880
Second, we obliterate the madness machine.

83
00:05:58,880 --> 00:06:01,540
And then, the madness relay stations.

84
00:06:02,300 --> 00:06:04,380
And finally, Arachne.

85
00:06:04,960 --> 00:06:07,280
Kill her and destroy her organization.

86
00:06:09,520 --> 00:06:10,440
Fine, then.

87
00:06:11,100 --> 00:06:12,760
They can ignore it all if they want.

88
00:06:13,440 --> 00:06:14,720
But they can't make me forget.

89
00:06:15,700 --> 00:06:18,220
We have every confidence in your skills.

90
00:06:18,820 --> 00:06:21,900
But we realize the risk of coming into contact with the Kishan.

91
00:06:22,420 --> 00:06:26,240
So do not forget to take your doses of madness suppressing before you leave.

92
00:06:28,880 --> 00:06:33,500
And now, a word from Lord Death.

93
00:06:33,500 --> 00:06:45,740
Do your best, okay?

94
00:06:46,280 --> 00:06:47,320
Victory, victory!

95
00:06:47,760 --> 00:06:48,600
That's it.

96
00:06:49,020 --> 00:06:49,960
Victory, victory!

97
00:06:50,800 --> 00:06:51,300
All right.

98
00:06:51,580 --> 00:06:53,160
The operation will now commence.

99
00:06:53,720 --> 00:06:56,180
First destination, Baba Yaga Castle.

100
00:06:56,180 --> 00:07:04,380
Excuse me, Mr. Cid.

101
00:07:04,800 --> 00:07:05,080
Hmm?

102
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:07,880
There's something I wanted to ask you.

103
00:07:08,540 --> 00:07:09,280
Go ahead.

104
00:07:10,220 --> 00:07:11,480
It's about Krona.

105
00:07:12,840 --> 00:07:14,540
What are they going to do with him?

106
00:07:15,540 --> 00:07:16,660
Please tell me.

107
00:07:16,860 --> 00:07:17,780
I know you know.

108
00:07:17,780 --> 00:07:17,860
No.

109
00:07:17,860 --> 00:07:23,200
Krona's been exiled, Maka.

110
00:07:24,640 --> 00:07:27,100
He was a spy and a traitor.

111
00:07:27,740 --> 00:07:29,600
He's done a lot of damage to the Academy.

112
00:07:30,200 --> 00:07:32,520
Given that, exile is lenient.

113
00:07:34,200 --> 00:07:34,760
Exile?

114
00:07:35,440 --> 00:07:36,980
But where can he go?

115
00:07:37,780 --> 00:07:40,160
When I was alive, I had tight lips.

116
00:07:40,160 --> 00:07:41,720
I knew how to keep a secret.

117
00:07:42,460 --> 00:07:44,300
That's the kind of man I was.

118
00:07:44,300 --> 00:07:47,580
But I did talk out loud to myself at times.

119
00:07:48,640 --> 00:07:50,940
Maybe Krona's exile is just a cover.

120
00:07:51,500 --> 00:07:54,720
Maybe he left with Miss Marie to go after Medusa.

121
00:07:55,280 --> 00:07:56,320
With Miss Marie?

122
00:07:56,880 --> 00:07:57,460
But why?

123
00:07:59,340 --> 00:08:01,400
Yesterday, Marie resigned.

124
00:08:01,780 --> 00:08:03,240
She's no longer with the Academy.

125
00:08:06,920 --> 00:08:10,240
Krona is going to settle things with Medusa once and for all.

126
00:08:11,300 --> 00:08:11,860
Medusa.

127
00:08:12,860 --> 00:08:13,900
It's all right.

128
00:08:14,300 --> 00:08:16,000
Miss Marie will be there to back him up.

129
00:08:16,620 --> 00:08:18,340
You should focus on today's operation.

130
00:08:22,560 --> 00:08:25,180
We're counting on you and your anti-magic wavelength.

131
00:08:25,840 --> 00:08:26,940
Don't let us down.

132
00:08:29,400 --> 00:08:30,440
So that's it.

133
00:08:31,440 --> 00:08:32,840
That's how they're going to handle it?

134
00:08:34,540 --> 00:08:36,400
This is the adult's great solution?

135
00:08:36,400 --> 00:08:36,460
This is the adult's great solution?

136
00:08:44,300 --> 00:08:51,160
Maka, I'm sorry.

137
00:08:51,520 --> 00:08:52,400
What is it, Krona?

138
00:08:52,640 --> 00:08:53,220
What's wrong?

139
00:08:54,300 --> 00:08:55,180
It's nothing.

140
00:08:56,120 --> 00:08:56,600
Fine.

141
00:08:56,820 --> 00:08:57,960
Then let's keep moving.

142
00:08:57,960 --> 00:09:04,000
I was in the same desert not long ago.

143
00:09:07,220 --> 00:09:08,840
I thought I was escaping.

144
00:09:12,060 --> 00:09:14,900
This time, this time it's different.

145
00:09:14,900 --> 00:09:26,240
Maka, I'm sorry I had to lie, but I'm not running anymore.

146
00:09:26,240 --> 00:09:35,800
We should split our forces into thirds and make our attack on three fronts.

147
00:09:36,460 --> 00:09:41,880
And the soldiers in charge of demolishing the relay stations need to synchronize their attacks so they all happen at one time.

148
00:09:41,880 --> 00:09:48,000
This is the first attack on so grand a scale since the academy was founded.

149
00:09:48,400 --> 00:09:52,000
That suppressant, do you really think it'll be effective against the madness?

150
00:09:52,740 --> 00:09:57,640
If such a medicine actually existed, I would have delivered it throughout the world already.

151
00:09:58,000 --> 00:09:58,900
I thought so.

152
00:09:59,640 --> 00:10:02,040
Suppressing panic, an obvious tactic.

153
00:10:04,520 --> 00:10:08,060
Lord Death, what I'd like to know is why I'm stationed here.

154
00:10:08,580 --> 00:10:10,200
Yeah, that is a good question.

155
00:10:10,200 --> 00:10:12,960
You were the one who made that call?

156
00:10:13,580 --> 00:10:17,400
Given what we're up against, I don't think we can have too many forces in the field.

157
00:10:18,060 --> 00:10:22,380
Based on my analysis, it wouldn't hurt to have all the death-sized fighting out there.

158
00:10:23,320 --> 00:10:25,140
Easier said than done, Azusa.

159
00:10:26,360 --> 00:10:26,800
Yikes!

160
00:10:27,540 --> 00:10:31,160
We're battling a Kishin today, yet for some reason you're keeping me here

161
00:10:31,160 --> 00:10:34,800
and you sent Marie and Kit off on assignments that have nothing to do with the fighting.

162
00:10:35,680 --> 00:10:37,880
If you ask me, it defies common sense.

163
00:10:37,880 --> 00:10:41,700
We can't know for sure what's going to happen on the battlefield today.

164
00:10:42,200 --> 00:10:46,380
Surely you'll agree the best plan of action is to prepare for all possibilities.

165
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:48,180
There, you see now?

166
00:10:48,320 --> 00:10:49,300
Not so simple.

167
00:10:51,080 --> 00:10:51,960
Oh, dear.

168
00:10:53,940 --> 00:10:57,380
Whatever they say, I still think our forces are too spread out.

169
00:10:57,380 --> 00:11:01,840
Why don't you put that scary face away and come have a cup of tea?

170
00:11:02,020 --> 00:11:02,660
Pull up a seat.

171
00:11:02,760 --> 00:11:04,300
There's some yummy cake over here.

172
00:11:04,720 --> 00:11:05,760
All right, you two!

173
00:11:05,960 --> 00:11:06,880
Shake off this!

174
00:11:09,040 --> 00:11:11,220
I don't know how to handle this woman.

175
00:11:12,480 --> 00:11:13,320
What was that?

176
00:11:13,320 --> 00:11:14,220
What's happening?

177
00:11:14,980 --> 00:11:17,660
Well, I'm sure things will sort themselves out.

178
00:11:17,880 --> 00:11:21,440
In the meantime, we'll focus on dealing with each new problem as it arises.

179
00:11:21,440 --> 00:11:25,540
Wonderful.

180
00:11:27,400 --> 00:11:31,100
I told Lord Death I wouldn't pause to accept some help.

181
00:11:31,360 --> 00:11:32,460
Hi, Mr. Joe.

182
00:11:32,560 --> 00:11:33,460
I'm Blair the Cat.

183
00:11:33,780 --> 00:11:35,600
Starting today, I'm your new assistant.

184
00:11:35,940 --> 00:11:36,720
Exciting, huh?

185
00:11:37,120 --> 00:11:38,800
I'm Lisa from Chupacabra.

186
00:11:38,960 --> 00:11:40,100
And my name's Arisa.

187
00:11:40,440 --> 00:11:43,400
But I don't think he quite understood my request.

188
00:11:43,400 --> 00:11:44,620
Meow, meow.

189
00:11:44,620 --> 00:11:51,840
We are now entering arachnophobious territory.

190
00:11:52,580 --> 00:11:55,040
All forces, make sure you're in place.

191
00:11:55,460 --> 00:11:56,920
Ready yourselves for the attack.

192
00:11:56,920 --> 00:12:15,020
Is there something bothering you, Maka?

193
00:12:15,680 --> 00:12:17,380
No, it's nothing.

194
00:12:18,320 --> 00:12:18,720
Uh-oh.

195
00:12:18,720 --> 00:12:20,500
You're not getting cold feet, are you?

196
00:12:20,660 --> 00:12:22,400
Because there's nothing to be afraid of.

197
00:12:22,500 --> 00:12:24,320
Not as long as I'm here, anyway.

198
00:12:24,320 --> 00:12:28,340
With a big star like me around, this is the safest place in the entire world.

199
00:12:29,780 --> 00:12:32,020
If you don't quiet down, they'll know we're here.

200
00:12:33,920 --> 00:12:36,300
Are you still thinking about that crap from last night?

201
00:12:37,600 --> 00:12:38,040
Maybe.

202
00:12:38,640 --> 00:12:40,600
You have to keep your head in the game today.

203
00:12:41,180 --> 00:12:42,900
Otherwise, the whole thing will fall apart.

204
00:12:43,040 --> 00:12:44,460
You of all people should know that.

205
00:12:47,500 --> 00:12:48,460
Don't worry, soul.

206
00:12:48,540 --> 00:12:50,460
I'm sure Maka's going to do really well today.

207
00:12:50,460 --> 00:12:54,040
Sid and Lord Death both set our anti-magic wavelengths might be all we need.

208
00:12:54,720 --> 00:12:56,940
They're counting on a technique I can't master.

209
00:12:57,560 --> 00:12:58,360
It's ridiculous.

210
00:12:59,500 --> 00:13:01,080
But there's more to it than that.

211
00:13:01,160 --> 00:13:03,760
The genie hunter's not the only thing that makes you a great fighter.

212
00:13:04,320 --> 00:13:06,200
There's nothing that great about me.

213
00:13:07,240 --> 00:13:07,760
Damn!

214
00:13:07,980 --> 00:13:09,500
Quit being such a perfectionist!

215
00:13:09,760 --> 00:13:11,220
Yeah, like that'll happen!

216
00:13:11,640 --> 00:13:13,360
Blackstar, will you please be quiet?

217
00:13:14,020 --> 00:13:15,600
Just leave me alone, guys.

218
00:13:15,600 --> 00:13:20,060
You had a conversation with Sid before we left, didn't you?

219
00:13:20,460 --> 00:13:22,500
What, you mean about the genie hunter move?

220
00:13:22,700 --> 00:13:24,080
I told you it's ridiculous.

221
00:13:24,200 --> 00:13:25,000
No, not that.

222
00:13:25,620 --> 00:13:27,060
About Miss Marie and Crona.

223
00:13:27,060 --> 00:13:31,800
Do you understand what's really going on?

224
00:13:32,280 --> 00:13:33,700
Why it had to be the two of them?

225
00:13:36,920 --> 00:13:39,400
The DWMA made a deal with Medusa.

226
00:13:39,820 --> 00:13:41,320
Because of that, we can't harm her.

227
00:13:41,940 --> 00:13:43,220
Lord Death gave his word not to.

228
00:13:44,620 --> 00:13:46,460
But Crona's in exile, isn't he?

229
00:13:46,680 --> 00:13:48,360
And Miss Marie quit her teaching job.

230
00:13:50,460 --> 00:13:52,940
Lord Death's making some pretty low moves these days.

231
00:13:53,640 --> 00:13:55,460
There might be something in what Kid told us.

232
00:13:55,700 --> 00:13:58,200
So maybe we really can't trust the Academy anymore.

233
00:14:00,860 --> 00:14:01,600
Sol's right.

234
00:14:01,920 --> 00:14:03,120
That's a sneaky plan.

235
00:14:04,600 --> 00:14:07,000
I was wondering why Kid's not here with us.

236
00:14:07,200 --> 00:14:08,940
Maybe this has something to do with it.

237
00:14:16,220 --> 00:14:20,000
We can't afford to freak out about every little thing that comes our way right now.

238
00:14:20,320 --> 00:14:22,080
If you ask me, it's the other way around.

239
00:14:22,080 --> 00:14:23,320
We can't afford not to.

240
00:14:24,440 --> 00:14:26,780
Don't know about you, but I'm here to win.

241
00:14:27,260 --> 00:14:29,460
I'm going to take down every last one of them.

242
00:14:29,860 --> 00:14:33,140
And when that's over, I'll surpass God.

243
00:14:34,660 --> 00:14:35,140
Great.

244
00:14:35,440 --> 00:14:36,360
Here he goes again.

245
00:14:39,600 --> 00:14:40,720
What should I do?

246
00:14:40,720 --> 00:14:55,360
You can sleep soundly, Asheron.

247
00:14:56,800 --> 00:14:57,700
It's okay.

248
00:14:58,300 --> 00:15:00,160
As long as I'm here by your side.

249
00:15:00,160 --> 00:15:12,600
You'll see, my dear one.

250
00:15:13,200 --> 00:15:17,680
Before much longer, the world will be utterly consumed by delicious madness.

251
00:15:18,800 --> 00:15:21,820
Until then, you'll stay here with me where you'll be safe.

252
00:15:21,820 --> 00:15:26,900
Lady Arachna, we have an issue.

253
00:15:27,400 --> 00:15:28,180
Let's hear it.

254
00:15:29,180 --> 00:15:31,740
We have detected DWMA forces.

255
00:15:32,980 --> 00:15:33,860
Oh, really?

256
00:15:34,660 --> 00:15:35,380
Yes, my lady.

257
00:15:35,580 --> 00:15:38,400
And it appears they're searching for a way into Baba Yaga Castle.

258
00:15:46,060 --> 00:15:47,220
So it would seem.

259
00:15:47,900 --> 00:15:50,680
They shouldn't have been able to find the castle's location, though.

260
00:15:50,680 --> 00:15:54,100
I don't think storming the castle is their only objective, either.

261
00:15:54,900 --> 00:15:58,260
They seem to have deployed six additional squads to other areas.

262
00:15:59,280 --> 00:16:00,300
Six forces?

263
00:16:00,880 --> 00:16:02,760
They're targeting the relay stations.

264
00:16:03,680 --> 00:16:06,660
The bulk of their forces will be arriving at our gates soon.

265
00:16:08,480 --> 00:16:09,820
How do they know?

266
00:16:14,200 --> 00:16:14,680
Medusa.

267
00:16:15,100 --> 00:16:16,200
It must have been.

